   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Caret Swap\n\nA gradient caret expands into a block that consumes the first text, then types the second.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2.2333 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- One phrase should be replaced by another through a caret gesture: the cursor swells into a block that eats the old text, collapses and types the new one.\n- A typewriter beat mid-scene without clearing to an empty frame.\n- A gradient caret should read as a character of its own, in an editor or AI-tool style.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You only need one phrase typed from empty: use typewriter.\n- The swap should happen word by word: use word-stream or value-swap.\n- A full-frame transition driven by a caret: use caret-wipe.\n\nVariables:\n- from_text (string): From text, default \"Executing it?\"\n- to_text (string): To text, default \"That's where everyone quits\"\n- font_size (number, 12-240): Font size, default 72\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"400\"\n- caret_color (color): Caret color, default \"#FF4DAA\"\n- caret_color_end (color): Caret color end, default \"#8A5CF6\"\n- swap_at (number, 0-60): Swap at, default 20\n- type_speed (number, 0.3-4): Type speed, default 1\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Caret Swap\n\n  A gradient caret expands into a block that consumes the first text, then types the second.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/caret-swap/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"caret-swap\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.2333\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"from_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"From text\", \"description\": \"Text that sits still until the caret eats it.\", \"default\": \"Executing it?\"},\n    {\"id\": \"to_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"To text\", \"description\": \"Text typed in after the swap.\", \"default\": \"That's where everyone quits\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 72, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"400\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"caret_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Caret color\", \"description\": \"Top of the caret gradient.\", \"default\": \"#FF4DAA\"},\n    {\"id\": \"caret_color_end\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Caret color end\", \"description\": \"Bottom of the caret gradient.\", \"default\": \"#8A5CF6\"},\n    {\"id\": \"swap_at\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Swap at\", \"description\": \"Frame at which the caret swells into a block.\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 60, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"type_speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Type speed\", \"description\": \"Frames for the first typed character; later gaps shrink.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.3, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Caret Swap</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { color: var(--color, #171717); font-family: Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; }\n        .cs-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; white-space: nowrap; }\n        .cs-row { position: relative; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; }\n        .cs-from { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n        .cs-caret { display: inline-block; flex-shrink: 0; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--c1, #FF4DAA), var(--c2, #8A5CF6)); }\n        .cs-ghost { visibility: hidden; }\n        .cs-over { position: absolute; top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); }\n        .cs-type { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 50%; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; white-space: pre; }\n        .cs-typed { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"caret-swap\" data-duration=\"2.2333\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"cs-clip\" class=\"cs-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.2333\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"cs-row\" class=\"cs-row\" role=\"img\">\n            <span id=\"cs-from\" class=\"cs-from\"></span>\n            <span id=\"cs-ghost\" class=\"cs-caret cs-ghost\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n            <span id=\"cs-over\" class=\"cs-caret cs-over\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n            <span id=\"cs-type\" class=\"cs-type\"><span id=\"cs-typed\" class=\"cs-typed\"></span><span id=\"cs-caret2\" class=\"cs-caret\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span></span>\n          </span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 to 1, rest at 0 velocity (mass, stiffness, damping), at `frame` of 30 fps.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            var TOTAL = 2.2333;\n            var FRAMES = Math.round(TOTAL * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function frameNow() { return Math.round(clock.frame * 1000) / 1000; }\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: FRAMES, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(frameNow()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"caret-swap\"] = tl;\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            function fit(el, size, frac, hfrac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxW = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              var maxH = Math.max(1, root.clientHeight * (hfrac || 0.9));\n              var k = Math.min(1, maxW / Math.max(1, el.scrollWidth), maxH / Math.max(1, el.scrollHeight));\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(8, size * k); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n\n\n            var fromText = str(vars.from_text, \"Executing it?\"), toText = str(vars.to_text, \"That's where everyone quits\");\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 240);\n            var swapAt = num(vars.swap_at, 20, 0, 60), typeSpeed = num(vars.type_speed, 1, 0.3, 4);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--c1\", str(vars.caret_color, \"#FF4DAA\"));\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--c2\", str(vars.caret_color_end, \"#8A5CF6\"));\n            var row = document.getElementById(\"cs-row\");\n            row.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"400\");\n            row.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", fromText + \" \" + toText);\n            var fromEl = document.getElementById(\"cs-from\"), typedEl = document.getElementById(\"cs-typed\");\n            var ghost = document.getElementById(\"cs-ghost\"), over = document.getElementById(\"cs-over\");\n            var typeWrap = document.getElementById(\"cs-type\"), caret2 = document.getElementById(\"cs-caret2\");\n            var CARET_LEAD = 7, EXPAND = 6, COLLAPSE = 7, IDLE = 7, BLINK = 8;\n            var CW = 0.08, CH = 1.1, GAP = 0.06, CHAR_W = 0.52, ACCEL = 0.96;\n            var toChars = Array.from(toText);\n            function typeElapsed(count) { return (typeSpeed * (1 - Math.pow(ACCEL, count))) / (1 - ACCEL); }\n            // Fit the font size to the wider of the two texts (measured on the row with that text).\n            fromEl.textContent = Array.from(fromText).length >= toChars.length ? fromText : toText;\n            size = fit(row, size, 0.9);\n            fromEl.textContent = fromText;\n            onFonts(function () { fromEl.textContent = Array.from(fromText).length >= toChars.length ? fromText : toText; size = fit(row, num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 240), 0.9); fromEl.textContent = fromText; layout(); });\n            var caretW, caretH;\n            function layout() {\n              caretW = CW * size; caretH = CH * size;\n              [ghost, over, caret2].forEach(function (c) { c.style.width = caretW + \"px\"; c.style.height = caretH + \"px\"; c.style.borderRadius = size * 0.03 + \"px\"; });\n              ghost.style.marginLeft = GAP * size + \"px\";\n              caret2.style.marginLeft = GAP * size + \"px\";\n            }\n            layout();\n            var caretVisibleAt = Math.max(swapAt - CARET_LEAD, 0);\n            var expandEnd = swapAt + EXPAND, collapseEnd = expandEnd + COLLAPSE;\n            var typeStart = collapseEnd + IDLE, typeEnd = typeStart + typeElapsed(toChars.length);\n            var expandE = bezier(0.6, 0, 0.8, 0.4), collapseE = bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.3, 1);\n            var anchorEm = Array.from(fromText).length * CHAR_W + CW + GAP;\n            var targetShiftEm = (anchorEm - toChars.length * CHAR_W) / 2;\n            start(function (raw) {\n              var frame = raw * speed;\n              var expand = ip(frame, swapAt, expandEnd, 0, 1, expandE);\n              var collapse = ip(frame, expandEnd, collapseEnd, 0, 1, collapseE);\n              var typing = frame >= typeStart;\n              var n = 0;\n              if (typing) while (n < toChars.length && typeElapsed(n) <= frame - typeStart) n++;\n              fromEl.style.visibility = frame < expandEnd ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n              over.style.display = typing ? \"none\" : \"block\";\n              typeWrap.style.display = typing ? \"inline-flex\" : \"none\";\n              if (!typing) {\n                var w, mask = \"none\";\n                over.style.left = \"auto\"; over.style.right = \"auto\";\n                if (frame < swapAt) { over.style.right = \"0px\"; w = caretW + \"px\"; }\n                else if (frame < expandEnd) { over.style.right = \"0px\"; w = \"calc(\" + (expand * 100).toFixed(3) + \"% + \" + ((1 - expand) * caretW).toFixed(2) + \"px)\"; }\n                else { over.style.left = \"0px\"; w = \"calc(\" + ((1 - collapse) * 100).toFixed(3) + \"% + \" + (collapse * caretW).toFixed(2) + \"px)\"; }\n                over.style.width = w;\n                if (frame >= swapAt) {\n                  var stop = frame < expandEnd ? 100 - 90 * expand : 10 + 90 * collapse;\n                  mask = \"linear-gradient(90deg, black \" + stop.toFixed(1) + \"%, transparent 100%)\";\n                }\n                over.style.webkitMaskImage = mask; over.style.maskImage = mask;\n                over.style.opacity = frame >= caretVisibleAt ? 1 : 0;\n              } else {\n                typedEl.textContent = toChars.slice(0, n).join(\"\");\n                var shift = targetShiftEm * (toChars.length > 0 ? n / toChars.length : 0) * size;\n                typeWrap.style.transform = \"translate(\" + shift.toFixed(1) + \"px, -50%)\";\n                var off = frame >= typeEnd + BLINK && Math.floor((frame - typeEnd) / BLINK) % 2 === 1;\n                caret2.style.opacity = off ? 0 : 1;\n              }\n            });\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
